#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:5 bda269b3c4a84b7f806b4d2721606409
msgid "Vibration Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:7 9dca5cc6ac7f4b23b341b7b7597ebaa6
msgid ""
"The vibration failsafe is a little different than most other failsafes in"
" ArduPilot, in that it does not initiate a flight mode change. Instead it"
" changes the algorithm which controls altitude and climb rate in altitude"
" control modes. It is enabled by default, but can be disabled by setting "
":ref:`FS_VIBE_ENABLE<FS_VIBE_ENABLE>` = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:10 99e6fdb9d6af49149b79910527450700
msgid "Impact of High Vibrations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:12 745b5962d93c4f9597b5ce635b1d9098
msgid ""
"Multicopters can suffer from very high vibration levels (more than "
"60m/s/s) which can lead to the accelerometers saturating (i.e. going "
"beyond the range that the sensor can measure). This leads to “clipping” "
"and means the EKF cannot accurately calculate its climb rate or vertical "
"acceleration. This can lead to the vehicle becoming unable to control its"
" climb rate and, in severe situations, can lead to the vehicle climbing "
"rapidly at full throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:15 c9d59507efa14a3997c9b5d668fa1596
msgid "When the failsafe will trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:17 109842a4cafd43c7bfd80387238dd4d5
msgid ""
"The vibration failsafe will trigger if all of the following are true for "
"at least one second:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:19 93292279b0544a738c5bcc42c4ef087b
msgid ""
"EKF’s vertical velocity innovations are positive (see onboard log's "
"XKF3.IVD value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:20 f42a8b5756ad4ef9ab6a2ac2b310d2a9
msgid "EKF's vertical position innovations are positive (see XKF3.IPD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:21 a19355cd8e2943d8903504601e6d167b
msgid "EKF's velocity variance is 1 or higher (see XKF4.SV)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:23 2412eb06888f4867a9ab2fea2b6de68d
msgid ""
"An ``Innovation`` is the difference between the predicted value and the "
"latest (non-IMU) value. A ``Variance`` is the EKF’s reported confidence "
"in its estimate. 0 is very good, >1 is bad."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:26 d48418d409564b32bec72abb8f709bf3
msgid "What will happen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:28 7729727cdd244e07b6e81a17c1fa6c71
msgid "If the vibration failsafe triggers the following will happen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:30 ae4c3942ed684e169273b4aa6c97244f
msgid ""
"“Vibration compensation ON” will appear on the Ground Stations HUD. EKF’s"
" climb rate will be calculated using a 3rd order complementary filter "
"which is tuned to be more resistant to vibration (but less accurate) than"
" the normal method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:31 5c9955b2649b499c8f29ff6c9700c392
msgid ""
"Altitude controller switches to a more vibration resistant two-stage "
"controller (position->velocity) instead of the regular three-stage "
"controller (i.e. position->velocity->acceleration)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:32 9071431bcc264e9483e0e3d4a427636e
msgid ""
"The vehicle will not change mode but its altitude hold will be less "
"accurate than normal. The vehicle may overshoot it’s altitude targets "
"and/or respond more slowly to pilot input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:35 2fdf04be38ed4837a9b7244d0052a10d
msgid "Recovery from the failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:37 058a71350a294ee8bfe4bb213e790be0
msgid ""
"Vibration failsafe will deactivate 15 seconds after the EKF returns to "
"normal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:38 1bb115e04f344f6597a52551c80c9142
msgid "“Vibration compensation OFF” will be displayed on the HUD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:39 9512242d20eb422b8c4674ef07957aad
msgid "Altitude and climb rate controllers will return to their normal methods"
msgstr ""

